{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 9,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.046,
            0.364,
            0.063
          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.088,
            0.848,
            0.146
          ],
          "content": "Even in this case, the area of rectangle AEFD can be found in two ways: (i) by directly using the side lengths n and (12 – 4), or (ii) subtracting the area of the rectangle EBCF from that of ABCD."
        },
        {
          "type": "chart",
          "bbox": [
            0.241,
            0.162,
            0.757,
            0.347
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_9_chart_2.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.363,
            0.848,
            0.419
          ],
          "content": "The first method gives us 8n, and the second method gives us $1 2 n - 4 n$ , and they are equal, since $12n - 4n = 8n$ . This is the expression for the area of the rectangle AEFD."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.419,
            0.847,
            0.474
          ],
          "content": "Sets of terms such as (5c, c, 10c), $(12n, -4n)$ that involve the same letter-numbers are called **like terms**. Sets of terms such as {18c, 11d} are called **unlike terms** as they have different letter-numbers."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.475,
            0.846,
            0.512
          ],
          "content": "As we have seen, like terms can be added together and simplified into a single term."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.52,
            0.532,
            0.598
          ],
          "content": "**Example 7:** A shop rents out chairs and tables for a day’s use. To rent them, one has to first pay the following amount per piece."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.542,
            0.51,
            0.843,
            0.592
          ],
          "content": "| Item | Amount |\n| --- | --- |\n| Chair | ₹40 |\n| Table | ₹75 |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_9_table_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.601,
            0.525,
            0.656
          ],
          "content": "When the furniture is returned, the shopkeeper pays back some amount as follows."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.657,
            0.525,
            0.712
          ],
          "content": "Write an expression for the total number of rupees paid if x chairs and y tables are rented."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.543,
            0.601,
            0.845,
            0.702
          ],
          "content": "|  | Amount returned |\n| --- | --- |\n| Chair | ₹6 |\n| Table | ₹10 |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_9_table_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.712,
            0.847,
            0.751
          ],
          "content": "For x chairs and y tables, let us find the total amount paid at the beginning and the amount one gets back after returning the furniture."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.758,
            0.602,
            0.781
          ],
          "content": "Describe the procedure to get these amounts."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.789,
            0.846,
            0.827
          ],
          "content": "The total amount in rupees paid at the beginning is $4 0 x \\pm 7 5 y$ , and the total amount returned is $6 x + 1 0 y .$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.827,
            0.676,
            0.847
          ],
          "content": "So, the total amount pai $\\mathbf{d} = (40x + 75y) - (6x + 10y).$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.854,
            0.761,
            0.878
          ],
          "content": "? Can we simplify this expression? If yes, how? If not, why not?"
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.818,
            0.838,
            0.905,
            0.891
          ],
